   "subject": "Re: Multiple Imputation Error: \"lavaan (0.5-22) model has NOT been fitted\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "It is not an error, it is a warning. As far as I can tell, everything \r<br>looks ok. The warning is produced by the &#39;summary()&#39; function, and is \r<br>most likely just a side-effect of the way semTools (0.4-13) creates the \r<br>lavaan object. I would not worry about it. Future updates of semTools \r<br>will (most likely) not create lavaan objects, and use a custom summary() \r<br>function.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>On 10/06/2016 05:45 PM, Alexander Neumann wrote:\r<br>&gt; Dear all,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I intend to run a CFA with multiple imputation using Lavaan 0.5-22 and\r<br>&gt; semTools 0.4-13. Curiously, no matter what model or dataset I use, I\r<br>&gt; always get following warning:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; **WARNING **lavaan (0.5-22)model has NOT been fitted **WARNING\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; **Estimatesbelow are simply the starting values\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Does anybody know the solution to this problem?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Below the example code from semTools and the corresponding output:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; library(lavaan)HS.model &lt;-&#39; visual =~ x1 + x2 + x3 textual =~ x4 + x5 +\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; x6 speed =~ x7 + x8 + x9\r<br>&gt; &#39;HSMiss&lt;-HolzingerSwineford1939[,paste(&quot;x&quot;,1:9,sep=&quot;&quot;)]randomMiss\r<br>&gt; &lt;-rbinom(prod(dim(HSMiss)),1,0.1)randomMiss\r<br>&gt; &lt;-matrix(as.logical(randomMiss),nrow=nrow(HSMiss))HSMiss[randomMiss]&lt;-NA\r<br>&gt; out&lt;-cfa.mi(HS.model,data=HSMiss,m =3,chi=&quot;all&quot;)summary(out)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; **WARNING **lavaan (0.5-22)model has NOT been fitted **WARNING\r<br>"
    ],
